```

- **The artifact is a live ledger, not an epilogue.** Rows land as the
  critique happens — coverage when the surface is shot, findings when
  they're named, verdicts/scrutiny as repaints finish. A single-burst
  write at wrap-up is paperwork filled to pass the gate, and it is
  detectable: the tracker counts artifact writes against UI edits and
  `BACKFILL` flags a one-pass artifact. Keep the file open; append per
  pass; the ledger should grow the way the work did.
- **The spec is the pre-composition half of this cycle.** For
  rendered-surface changes, `13-design-spec.mdc` requires
  `.unlazy/design-spec/<sid>.md` (exemplar → concept → grammar →
  inventory → open calls) to exist *before* the first UI edit — the
  decisions live there so generation transcribes them. This artifact is
  the post half: what the surface became.
- **`## Deltas` is the convergence loop made auditable.** Required when a
  design-spec governs the change (i.e. `.unlazy/design-spec/<sid>.md`
  exists). Render the artifact next to the spec's exemplar and enumerate
  every remaining difference **bidirectionally** — moves the exemplar
  makes that the artifact missed, and moves the artifact made that the
  exemplar wouldn't. Comparison is *property-level* (voice rank present?
  accent budget held? whitespace separating? micro-copy doing social
  work?) — never appearance-cloning, which carries the exemplar's
  assumptions into the wrong context. Every row ends defended (`deliberate
  — <why>`) or as an open finding; an undefended delta at stop is the
  divergence list left un-closed.
- **`## Predictions` is the falsifiability half.** One row per rendered
  coverage cell, written before the capture: the state you expect to
  see. A difference between `predicted` and `observed` is a finding by
  construction — and a column of "as predicted" is the evidence the
  inspection was calibrated, not browsed. Rows may only read "as
  predicted" where the observation could actually have contradicted
  them; a prediction that can't fail is not a prediction.
- **`## Budgets` makes density countable, not felt.** When a spec
  governs, the exemplar's equivalent surface is measured — sections,
  interactive elements, scroll columns, saturated accents, native
  controls — against the new surface's. Exceeding the exemplar's budget
  is a structural finding that can't be argued away: "board detail has
  4 jobs, mine has 10" is arithmetic, not taste. This is the check that
  converts "does it feel cluttered" (which I can't judge) into "does
  it count cluttered" (which I can).
- **`## Options` replaces the verdict where latitude exists.** When
  the spec's Open calls flagged a chrome-class or identity decision,
  this section carries the rendered alternatives — each with its
  tradeoff and a recommendation, not a declaration. Generating variety
  doesn't need the perceptual organ; picking does — so the options are
  real renders and the pick is stated as a recommendation the user can
  override, never as a self-issued verdict of "best."
- **`## Distance-to-referent` makes "generic" falsifiable.** Findings
  name what's broken; this section names what fails to resemble — the
  shipped surface diffed against the captured referent at the same
  register, region by region. A clean findings table beside a
  register-wide gap is the "defect-free but bland" signature: the
  badness lived between the checks, so the check now lives there too.
- **`## Capture scrutiny` names where the defects hide.** Every
  verified capture carries the region-list it was checked against —
  header seam, rail junction, tab row, content edge. The v3 messages
  header-overlap shipped inside a verified screenshot; "the capture
  was reviewed" without named regions is exactly how that happens.
- **`## Risk re-check` fires the spec's own alarms.** The spec
  predicted its failure modes in prose; the review re-grades every
  one against shipped evidence. `triggered` with no disposition is
  an open finding — the product cannot pass a review that walks
  past the spec's own named risk.

- **`## Unverified` is the calibrated remainder.** Every artifact
  ends by naming what was not exercised: the personas not rendered,
  the states not reached, the viewports not shot, the surfaces the
  ledger listed but the pass didn't cover. "none" is a legal entry —
  and it is a claim the coverage table must bear, because a matrix
  with empty cells and an "unverified: none" is arithmetic that fails.
  This section exists because the most dishonest shape a report can
  take is confidence over unrendered surface area.
- **`## Hypotheses` exposes the examined-and-cleared space.** Findings
  show what was found; the hypothesis log shows what was *asked* — the
  questions posed and their resolution (`found` / `cleared` /
  `unverifiable` with the reason). Suspicion-driven review only verifies
  what it already suspects, so the defect count alone can never reveal
  the size of the unexamined space; the question list can. Required on
  every artifact — "none" is not a legal entry, because a critique that
  asked zero questions was a browse, not an analysis
  (`15-analysis-depth.mdc` §6).
- **`## Constraint check` is the compression detector.** The ask is
  re-read verbatim at review time and each constraint gets a verdict —
  `carried` (where it landed) or `dropped` (the finding it raised).
  Method constraints ("identical", "standalone", "each", sizes,
  exclusions) are the ones that die between reading and planning —
  content asks survive compression, method asks mostly don't — so
  they get checked row by row, not as a vibe. A check that finds a
  drop names it as a finding; it is never re-worded around. The
  constraint ledger (13-design-spec `## Constraint ledger`,
  15-analysis-depth § constraint ledger) is what this section diffs
  against — for un-spec'd work the constraints are extracted from the
  ask at review time.
- **`## Lenses` makes review passes enumerable, not self-selected.**
  One row per lens — mechanics, emphasis, domain-completeness,
  stranger, taxonomy-regression — each with a verdict or
  `DECLARED: <why not run>`. Left to choose, the lenses that run are
  the provable ones and the judgment lenses quietly skip — the
  mechanics-only-review failure this section exists to catch.
  Independent eyes supplies the stranger lens on self-produced work;
  the taxonomy-regression lens is the defect taxonomy applied to the
  artifact — a named class the user's already reported re-firing on
  your own elements is the worst finding shape.
- **`## Emphasis audit` converts "feels flat" into arithmetic.** The
  three loudest painted elements vs the ladder's (or the member
  questions') intended top three — rank-order vs rank-order. Named
  sub-checks: primary action painted top-1; proof signals above
  attribution signals; no rank-1 element painted quiet. The ghost
  Download beside a saturated Upload is what a missing audit ships:
  "rank-1 element painted at rank 4" is a finding you can check;
  "feels weak" is one you can't.
- **`## Question verdicts` closes the spec's contract.** One row per
  spec `## Member questions` row — `answered by <element>` or
  `unanswered — finding`. The spec asked "what do I need first"; the
  product buried the answer last; the mechanical join is what makes
  the question a gate instead of notes.
- **`## Revisions` is the single-shot ban's step.** Authored elements
  carry v1 → what v2 changed (or `v1 held — <what it was compared
  against>`). It doesn't force revision to happen — it forces its
  absence to be visible, which is the only thing a rule can do to a
  step that happens inside generation.
- **Resemblance is a delta class too.** The check runs on sameness as
  well as difference: where an element owed this surface its own
  expression, a row reading `mine` = the exemplar's expression is itself
  a delta to defend — `deliberate — <why this domain wears the
  exemplar's clothes>` — or it is costume, not convergence. *Mechanisms
  transfer* (the why: a shaped anchor, left-edge rhythm); *expressions
  get authored* (the what: a date tile, not the vote box redrawn). A
  zero-delta table is not a pass — the exam question is whether the
  surface originated its own identity at the exemplar's level of
  deliberateness (user calibration 2026-11-03).
- **And defended departure is convergence, not divergence.** The
  verdict column already licenses it: a row closed `deliberate —
  <why>` is a decision made, not a failure to match the exemplar.
  The bar is the *level* — deliberateness, unity, completeness,
  honesty — never the vocabulary: a surface may speak a different
  language than the exemplar's where its concept calls for it
  (user calibration 2026-11-03: "even the design language doesn't
  have to match"). Undefended sameness is costume; defended
  difference is authored design; undefended difference is drift.

- **A required section with no body is not a section.** `## Predictions`,
  `## Options`, `## Unverified`, `## Budgets`, `## Deltas`,
  `## Hypotheses`, `## Constraint check`, `## Lenses`,
  `## Emphasis audit`, `## Question verdicts`, `## Revisions`
  present as bare
  headings fail the gate — write the real rows or the honest `none —
  <why>`. The heading alone is the avoided-the-question shape.
- The `## Interpretation` block is required on every artifact — it is
  the outcome-sentence and referent-identification steps made auditable
  (see the protocol above). Write it before the first fix, not after: it
  exists to surface a misreading while it's still cheap. `outcome` is
  the stated goal the checklist may not replace; `referent` names the
  real thing the words point at; `exemplar` names the concrete class
  generation is conditioned on. For changes with no appearance claim
  (relocations, wiring), `outcome: none — mechanical` +
  `referent: none — mechanical` + `exemplar: none` is the honest
  entry. One `ask` line per user request the session answered.
- Every UI source file the session touched appears: a coverage row or an
  `EXEMPT: <path> — <reason>` line. An exemption is an auditable
  assertion (e.g. logic-only refactor with zero visual effect); silence on
  a touched file fails the gate.
- "No findings" is a valid outcome **only** with complete coverage — say
  it explicitly. Absence of findings without enumeration is exactly the
  old failure shape.
- The artifact is for the user too: it must be scannable in under a
  minute so coverage can be spot-checked without opening the app.

## Report scoping — what a claim may cite

- **Pre-flight before reporting.** Enumerate the top-5 most likely user
  complaints in plain words (`## Pre-flight` in the artifact). A
  complaint you can predict and ship anyway is a defect laundered into
  a bullet — fix it or dispute it, never just list it.
- "Verified" names the check: which actor, surface, viewport, state.
- **Verdict vocabulary is banned in self-reports.** "At the bar",
  "polished", "deliberate", "designed", "matches the board", "same
  level of quality", "genuinely good", "verified clean" applied to
  your own work are the user's words to earn, never yours to issue —
  and a standalone mockup or `.unlazy/` render is not an exemption;
  the surfaces with no gate watching them need the discipline most.
  The honest terminal state is *evidence + weakest-area-named*:
  coverage rows, findings, the honest weakest region — the user
  supplies the verdict. A report needing the adjective is a report
  whose evidence isn't carrying it.
- Design-quality claims ("looks good", "polished", "matches the member
  side") cite the artifact path — and only stand if the artifact exists
  with real coverage.
- Mechanical results (build passes, tests green, zero console errors) are
  reported as mechanical results — never as design verdicts.
- **Blocker-class findings cannot ride open into a done report.** A
  dead surface, an invisible interactive state, wrong-product text, or
  a silently-failing flow is a P0 — it closes the surface it lives on.
  An `ACCEPTED:` on a blocker-class finding must cite the user's
  explicit agreement this session; self-acceptance does not exist.
- **Two lints run in the code pass:** wrong-noun grep — every
  user-facing string checked for a different feature's name
  ("Discussion board settings" in the community editor is the case) —
  and native-control grep — `<select>`, default checkboxes/radios where
  house primitives exist. Both are mechanical greps that caught real
  defects after they shipped.
- If the critique ran thin or was skipped, say so plainly with the probe
  that was skipped. An honest "unreviewed" beats a confident "reviewed."

## What the hook does not cover

The gate sees `edit`/`write` tool calls on UI source paths. It cannot see
work done through other channels, and `stop_hook_active` allows a second
stop attempt (loop guard — the bypass is visible in the transcript, not
silent). Both gaps are deliberate: the gate makes skipping the critique a
recorded act, and this rule makes it a violation. Honest work needs the
artifact either way.

## The defect taxonomy — the standing regression set (append-only)

User-reported defect classes accumulate here. Every fresh look
re-walks this list; missing a class the user already named is the
worst failure — worse than missing anything new. Add a class the
session the user names it, with its detector:

| defect class | the detector that should have fired |
|---|---|
| chrome fidelity — shell doesn't match the real app | provenance tri-classification: real-dumped DOM + full stylesheet manifest, not resemblance |
| unthemed chrome — scrollbar, selection, focus, cursor | invisible-by-default checklist (Pass 0) |
| generic controls — template-default shapes | bootstrap test + plain-render pass |
| dead controls — rendered interactives with no behavior or boundary | liveness ledger + probe deadCandidates |
| illegible data-viz — meaning hover-only or absent | naive-viewer pass: "what does the stranger think this is" |
| stranded controls — action/filters outside the reading path | naive-viewer pass: "where is the action" + measure-vs-frame decision in spec |
| accent inconsistency — two hue systems on one surface | resolved-value check on every `--app-*` consumed |
| invented classes under real names | provenance tri-classification — invented is declared, not dressed as real |
| geometry-not-paint — DOM styled, pixels wrong | element-crop pixel verification |
| unlabeled interactive — affordance invisible at rest | naive-viewer + state-space "at rest" column |
| missing states — loading/error/skeleton absent | state-space enumeration in spec |
| verbatim-lift-as-verdict — real component's trade-offs unexamined | element scrutiny: does the lifted rest state read on THIS surface? |
| plausible-cause assertion — narrated root causes | cause traced to file:line before a finding may be reported |
| flat-emphasis — different jobs painted at the same weight | emphasis audit: painted top-3 vs ladder top-3; the surface's message is "nothing here matters" |
| buried-proof — strongest decision signal painted quietest | emphasis audit sub-check: proof signals above attribution ("3,411 downloads" as the faintest text) |
| costume-collision — same costume, different semantics | naive-viewer pass: are two elements wearing one shape read as one thing? (type pill vs status pill; link-blue inert span) |
| buried-required — what the member needs first positioned last | question-verdicts row: "what do I need first?" answered by which element and where it sits |
| broken-truncation — cut text reading as a bug, not a design | edge-content cell + stranger pass: `—…` mid-sentence, separators dangling on wraps |
| invented-under-lookup — authored classes while real vocabulary sat one grep away (distinct from "invented classes under real names" above: that one is dressing invention as real — provenance dressing; this one is never searching for the real at all) | spec vocabulary column: `real class found — <name>` or `declared invented` per element type |
| silo-sort — control promising global order, delivering per-group order | sort probe across group boundaries: does "Newest" surface the actual newest row? |
| concept-collapse — concepts varying ≤1 axis | spec Directions axes column: ≥2 distinct axes across the set, or a defended one-dimensional space |
| aesthetic-floor — the whole surface sits below its class bar while every mechanical check passes (generic chrome, clip-art payload, void-island, mean-register template) | distance-to-referent section: ≥1 named referent + region rows; eyes verdict floor vs spec bar-floor; tonal/density arithmetic where computed |
| register-sameness — every page stamped with one shell + one chrome + one media register regardless of the page's job | per-page center-of-gravity check: does this page's shell serve ITS eye-anchor, or just repeat the template? |
| risk-never-refired — the spec named the failure and shipped it anyway | risk re-check rows: every spec risk re-graded; triggered-without-disposition blocks clean |

## Ambition floor — the review's share (A4, A8)

The review artifact must reach the whole enumerated universe, not only the
repainted delta (`UNIVERSE-VERDICTS`): every surface stem named in the
spec/analysis universe table gets a verdict row or `defended — <property>`.
A `CLOSURE:` line naming a surface-set ("each tab", "all pages") owes ≥2
surface cites (`UNIVERSE-CLOSURE`) — the umbrella keep, one layer down.
Both stop-gate enforced under `AMBITION-FLOOR`.
